[
  {
    "pkheadingid": 457,
    "bookid": 34,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Definition",
    "headingPosition": 1,
    "headingid": 370,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 65559,
        "bookId": 34,
        "chapterId": 412,
        "headingId": 370,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>Burkitt lymphoma (BL) is an aggressive B-cell lymphoma characterized by frequent presentation in extranodal sites or as acute leukaemia, with high proliferative activity and usually <em>MYC</em> translocation.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2020-06-10T10:08:47"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 458,
    "bookid": 34,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "ICD-O coding",
    "headingPosition": 2,
    "headingid": 371,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 65560,
        "bookId": 34,
        "chapterId": 412,
        "headingId": 371,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>9687/3 Burkitt lymphoma NOS</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2020-06-10T10:08:47"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 459,
    "bookid": 34,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "ICD-11 coding",
    "headingPosition": 3,
    "headingid": 372,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 65561,
        "bookId": 34,
        "chapterId": 412,
        "headingId": 372,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>2A85.6 &amp; XH3FE9 Burkitt lymphoma, including Burkitt leukaemia &amp; Mature B-cell lymphomas</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2020-06-10T10:08:47"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 460,
    "bookid": 34,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Related terminology",
    "headingPosition": 4,
    "headingid": 373,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 65562,
        "bookId": 34,
        "chapterId": 412,
        "headingId": 373,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>Burkitt cell leukaemia</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2020-06-10T10:08:47"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 461,
    "bookid": 34,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Subtype(s)",
    "headingPosition": 5,
    "headingid": 374,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 65563,
        "bookId": 34,
        "chapterId": 412,
        "headingId": 374,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>Sporadic Burkitt lymphoma; endemic Burkitt lymphoma; immunodeficiency-associated Burkitt lymphoma</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2020-06-10T10:08:47"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 462,
    "bookid": 34,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Localization",
    "headingPosition": 6,
    "headingid": 375,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 65564,
        "bookId": 34,
        "chapterId": 412,
        "headingId": 375,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>All organs of the female genital tract can be involved, with ovarian involvement accounting for most cases {28284518; 16224219; 11444509}.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2020-06-10T10:08:47"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 463,
    "bookid": 34,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Clinical features",
    "headingPosition": 7,
    "headingid": 376,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 65565,
        "bookId": 34,
        "chapterId": 412,
        "headingId": 376,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>Patients often present acutely with bulky disease.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2020-06-10T10:08:47"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 464,
    "bookid": 34,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Epidemiology",
    "headingPosition": 8,
    "headingid": 377,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 65566,
        "bookId": 34,
        "chapterId": 412,
        "headingId": 377,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>BL accounts for 5&ndash;20% of lymphomas involving the female genital tract {28284518; 16224219; 11444509}. Endemic BL occurs in equatorial Africa and in Papua New Guinea, with a peak incidence in children aged 4&ndash;7&nbsp;years {13628987; 4342309}. Sporadic BL is seen throughout the world, mainly in children and young adults {22488262}. Immunodeficiency-associated BL is mostly seen in the setting of HIV infection {1987908}.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2020-06-10T10:08:47"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 465,
    "bookid": 34,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Etiology",
    "headingPosition": 9,
    "headingid": 378,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 65567,
        "bookId": 34,
        "chapterId": 412,
        "headingId": 378,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>Infectious agents (e.g. EBV, <em>Plasmodium falciparum</em>, and HIV), environmental factors, and genetic predispositions are known etiological cofactors.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2020-06-10T10:08:47"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 466,
    "bookid": 34,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Pathogenesis",
    "headingPosition": 10,
    "headingid": 379,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 65568,
        "bookId": 34,
        "chapterId": 412,
        "headingId": 379,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>EBV infection is the main pathogenic factor in 90% of endemic BL cases and 20&ndash;40% of sporadic and immunodeficiency-associated BL cases {210392; 24434689; 22260300; 8392401; 1868025}. The molecular hallmark of BL is deregulation of MYC expression by translocation of <em>MYC</em> to an IG gene locus. Gene expression profiling has defined characteristic molecular signatures for BL {16760443; 16760442}. Mutations of <em>TCF3</em> (<em>E2A</em>) and <em>ID3</em> are seen in 70% of sporadic BL cases {23143597; 23143595; 22885699; 22897848}. Mutations of <em>MYC</em>, <em>CCND3</em>, <em>TP53</em>, <em>RHOA</em>, <em>SMARCA4</em>, and <em>ARID1A</em> are found in 5&ndash;40% of BL cases {23091298}.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2020-06-10T10:08:47"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 473,
    "bookid": 34,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Macroscopic appearance",
    "headingPosition": 11,
    "headingid": 386,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 65569,
        "bookId": 34,
        "chapterId": 412,
        "headingId": 386,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>Bulky masses in extranodal involvement of ovaries are seen.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2020-06-10T10:08:47"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 467,
    "bookid": 34,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Histopathology",
    "headingPosition": 12,
    "headingid": 380,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 65570,
        "bookId": 34,
        "chapterId": 412,
        "headingId": 380,
        "headingText": "<p>BL is characterized by diffuse sheets of monotonous medium-sized lymphoid cells with high mitotic activity and apoptosis, resulting in a starry-sky pattern due to the presence of numerous tingible-body macrophages. The tumour cells express B-cell antigens (CD19, CD20, CD22, CD79a, PAX5), germinal-centre markers (CD10, BCL6, CD38), and MYC but not BCL2, CD5, CD23, CD138, or&nbsp;TdT {15258997; 10191768; 21718280; 29954940}. The Ki-67 proliferation index is high, virtually 100%.</p>",
        "timestamp": "2020-08-04T15:48:13"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 468,
    "bookid": 34,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Cytology",
    "headingPosition": 13,
    "headingid": 381,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 65571,
        "bookId": 34,
        "chapterId": 412,
        "headingId": 381,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>When ovaries are involved, the neoplastic cells can be identified in peritoneal fluid.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2020-06-10T10:08:47"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 469,
    "bookid": 34,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Diagnostic molecular pathology",
    "headingPosition": 14,
    "headingid": 382,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 65572,
        "bookId": 34,
        "chapterId": 412,
        "headingId": 382,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p><em>MYC</em> translocation can be demonstrated.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2020-06-10T10:08:47"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 472,
    "bookid": 34,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Essential and desirable diagnostic criteria",
    "headingPosition": 15,
    "headingid": 385,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 65573,
        "bookId": 34,
        "chapterId": 412,
        "headingId": 385,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p><em>Essential:</em> a diffuse monotonous infiltrate of medium-sized lymphoid cells with squared-off contours, round nuclei with finely clumped chromatin, multiple nucleoli, and basophilic cytoplasm; numerous mitotic figures and apoptotic bodies; immunophenotype: B-lineage marker positivity, CD10+, BCL6+, BCL2&minus;, MYC+ (&gt;&nbsp;80%), and Ki-67+ (&gt;&nbsp;95%).</p>\r\n<p><em>Desirable:</em> demonstration of <em>MYC</em> gene rearrangement by FISH.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2020-06-10T10:08:47"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 470,
    "bookid": 34,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Staging",
    "headingPosition": 16,
    "headingid": 383,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 65574,
        "bookId": 34,
        "chapterId": 412,
        "headingId": 383,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>BL is staged according to the Lugano staging system.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2020-06-10T10:08:47"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 471,
    "bookid": 34,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Prognosis and prediction",
    "headingPosition": 17,
    "headingid": 384,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 65575,
        "bookId": 34,
        "chapterId": 412,
        "headingId": 384,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>BL is a highly aggressive but potentially curable (with intensive chemotherapy) tumour. Adverse prognostic factors include advanced-stage disease, bulky tumour, and high serum LDH levels {22260323; 23913575; 27136063}.</p>",
        "timestamp": "2020-06-10T10:08:47"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  }
]